From ceb53bb9b7e59f8d50f5b4790dd569ad9f0af824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:08:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09932/11362] Receipts over evidence read the working tree, not
 the artifact's commit

REQ-REPORT-6610 pins a receipt to the bytes at the artifact's own commit. That
is right for a shared capability spec, which churns because spec-first
discipline makes it churn. Applied to a file under results/ it is wrong, and
measurably so.

Mutating an upstream artifact three ways and rebuilding exp5342:

  utility_memory_ready changed  -> 19 content fields move; caught without a receipt
  flagged_adversarial added     -> NO content field moves; receipt-only
  hand-written note dropped     -> NO content field moves; receipt-only

The last two are this project's own incidents: the fabrication gate stamping a
landed artifact, and a test run dropping inference_substrate_correction_note
from exp3946. Under a pinned receipt both are green, and nothing else reports
them.

So _resolve now answers from the working tree for a path under results/ unless
the caller passes allow_evidence_pin=True. Raising instead was written first and
rejected: a hard error makes every honest caller pass the override to get
working code, producing pinned evidence receipts everywhere -- the outcome the
rule exists to prevent. The safe behaviour therefore needs no caller action.

Spec: REQ-REPORT-6610-EVIDENCE-LIVE and SCENARIO-REPORT-6610-EVIDENCE-LIVE,
appended, with the rejected alternative recorded so it is not re-proposed.

Also appended a correction: the Implementation Status row claimed adoption by
the replay-tested modules. That was not true. A grep for the word
provenance_receipts matched an unrelated artifact FIELD of the same name in
three modules; no module imported the helper. Appended rather than edited, per
never-prune.

Mutation-proved in a git worktree with module resolution verified by import
(m.__file__ under the worktree, not the editable install). 18 pass; delete the
guard -> RED; narrow _EVIDENCE_PREFIXES to a directory nothing matches -> RED;
drop the allow_evidence_pin condition -> RED; restore -> 18 pass. The second
mutation is the pattern-list-narrower-than-its-concept case, so that failure
mode is under test rather than assumed.

The fall-through-instead-of-raise refinement in _resolve came from a teammate
working the same task; this commit keeps it and aligns the spec and tests to it,
which were still describing my original raising design.

Staged via the index so the co-resident REQ-REPORT-6605 work in this spec file,
which belongs to another agent and whose test file is not yet committed, stays
uncommitted in the working tree.

